        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Measure the slab, take the low end of the coverage range for your chemistry, multiply out the coats properly, and round up to the next container. That sequence produces a number you can buy against, and it is almost always one container more than the label arithmetic suggests.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The gallon you do not use costs a few dollars and sits on a shelf. The gallon you are missing costs you a visible seam, a strip that fails early, and a second afternoon. Buy the spare.
          </p>
        </div>

